1
00:06:32,307 --> 00:06:38,307
Heavenly Sword is a adventure, action, animation film directed by Jang Gun-ho.

2
00:13:04,615 --> 00:13:10,615
The film's plot follows that of the game closely.

3
00:19:36,923 --> 00:19:42,923
Nariko, a member of an ancient tribe who have guarded an ancient magical sword for thousands of years, is charged
with bringing the sword to its destined wielder, a deity reincarnated who will bring peace to the land.

4
00:26:09,230 --> 00:26:15,230
But on her quest, Nariko must wield the sword herself against the forces
of King Bohan, who wishes to possess the weapon himself.

5
00:32:41,538 --> 00:32:47,538
Nariko (voice), played by Anna Torv.

6
00:39:13,846 --> 00:39:19,846
King Bohan (voice), played by Alfred Molina.

7
00:45:46,153 --> 00:45:52,153
Loki (voice), played by Thomas Jane.

8
00:52:18,461 --> 00:52:24,461
Kai (voice), played by Ashleigh Ball.

9
00:58:50,769 --> 00:58:56,769
Flying Fox / Prophet Takashi (voice), played by Barry Dennen.

10
01:05:23,076 --> 01:05:29,076
Whiptail, Old Woman (voice), played by Renae Geerlings.

11
01:11:55,384 --> 01:12:01,384
Heavenly Sword is a 2014 American adult animated action-adventure fantasy film based on the
2007 video game of the same name, developed by companies Sony and Ninja Theory.

12
01:18:27,692 --> 01:18:33,692
It was released digitally, and theatrically in selected regions.
